   "evidence": "Lines 147-167: `longitudinal`, `longitudinal_def`, `nPlus_mem_longitudinal`, `nMinus_mem_longitudinal` are the only API; grep for `mem_longitudinal` in the file hits no iff. The file's own proof at lines 228-235 does exactly this unfolding (`rw [longitudinal_def, Submodule.mem_span_pair]`), confirmed as `Submodule.mem_span_pair` at Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Span/Defs.lean:518 (not `@[simp]`).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/LightConeBasis.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] theorem mem_longitudinal_iff {v : V} : v \u2208 L.longitudinal \u2194 L.transverseProj v = 0` (from `ker_transverseProj_eq_longitudinal` + `LinearMap.mem_ker`), or the span-pair form `\u2194 \u2203 a b : R, a \u2022 L.nPlus + b \u2022 L.nMinus = v`.",
   "issue": "`longitudinal` is public but has no `mem_longitudinal_iff`; deciding `v \u2208 L.longitudinal` forces a consumer to unfold via `longitudinal_def` + `Submodule.mem_span_pair`, while the dual `transverse` gets `@[simp] mem_transverse_iff` (line 171).",
   "line": 147
